      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To find the area of the square, we first need to determine the length of one side of the square. Given the perimeter, we can use the formula for the perimeter of a square:\n\nPerimeter = 4 × side length\n\nWe are given that the perimeter is 32 feet, so we can set up the equation:\n\n32 = 4 × side length\n\nTo find the side length, we divide both sides of the equation by 4:\n\nside length = 32 / 4\nside length = 8 feet\n\nNow that we know the side length of the square is 8 feet, we can find the area by using the formula for the area of a square:\n\nArea = side length × side length\n\nSubstitute the side length we found into the formula:\n\nArea = 8 × 8\nArea = 64 square feet\n\nTherefore, the area of the square is \\boxed{64} square feet.",
