      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the area of a square, we use the formula:\n\n\\[ \\text{Area} = \\text{side}^2 \\]\n\nFirst, we need to determine the length of one side of the square. We know the perimeter of the square is 32 feet. The perimeter \\( P \\) of a square is given by:\n\n\\[ P = 4 \\times \\text{side} \\]\n\nLet's denote the side length of the square as \\( s \\). Therefore, we can write:\n\n\\[ 32 = 4s \\]\n\nTo find \\( s \\), we divide both sides of the equation by 4:\n\n\\[ s = \\frac{32}{4} = 8 \\]\n\nSo, the side length of the square is 8 feet. Now, we can find the area of the square by squaring the side length:\n\n\\[ \\text{Area} = s^2 = 8^2 = 64 \\]\n\nTherefore, the area of the square is:\n\n\\[ \\boxed{64} \\]",
