    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find the area of a square with a given perimeter, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Determine the side length of the square.\n2. Calculate the area using the side length.\n\nStep 1: Determine the side length of the square.\nThe perimeter \\( P \\) of a square is given by the formula:\n\\[ P = 4s \\]\nwhere \\( s \\) is the side length of the square. We are given that the perimeter is 32 feet. Therefore, we can set up the equation:\n\\[ 4s = 32 \\]\nTo find \\( s \\), we divide both sides of the equation by 4:\n\\[ s = \\frac{32}{4} = 8 \\]\nSo, the side length of the square is 8 feet.\n\nStep 2: Calculate the area of the square.\nThe area \\( A \\) of a square is given by the formula:\n\\[ A = s^2 \\]\nSubstituting the side length \\( s = 8 \\) into the formula, we get:\n\\[ A = 8^2 = 64 \\]\nTherefore, the area of the square is:\n\\[ \\boxed{64} \\]",
